I'll explore the chat input components to understand how attachments flow.I have the full picture. Attachments are already audio-aware (`ChatAttachment.isAudio()`, `ChatAttachmentPreview` renders an `<audio>` player), and `Chat.vue` already converts uploaded `File`s into `ChatAttachment` via `@upload-files`. So the missing piece is a **recorder in the composer** that emits an audio `File` through the existing `upload-files` channel — no changes needed anywhere else.

## 1. Review & Understand

- **Goal:** let the user record a voice note from the chat input and send it as an attachment.
- **Reuse, don't add:** `ChatAttachment.fromFile` (in `Chat.vue → prepareAttachmentFromFile`) + `@upload-files` + `ChatAttachmentPreview` (audio player) already cover storage, preview, edit and removal.
- **Constraints:** Vue Options API, Tailwind/DaisyUI only, no `<style>`, no semicolons, `<script setup>` imports only, must keep mobile collapse behaviour intact.
- **Edge cases:** unsupported browser, mic permission denied, cancel recording, max duration, unmount/collapse while recording, Safari mime fallback (`audio/mp4`).

## 2. Changes Summary

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/components/chat/ChatInputBox.vue` | Add a compact voice-note bar (record → timer → Attach / Cancel). MediaRecorder lifecycle in `data`/`methods`, emits the recorded audio `File` through the existing `upload-files` event, cleanup on unmount/collapse, `Escape` cancels. |

