## 4. Why this shape

- **Single source of truth.** MediaRecorder, timers and mic release stay in `ChatInputBox`; the toolbar is a pure presentational control, so no stream state leaks into a child that unmounts on mobile collapse.
- **Recording controls are always reachable.** The timer pill + Attach/Cancel sit *before* the `isEditing` / normal branches, so the recording can never be hidden by an edit-mode or search-state switch.
- **Toolbar visual language kept.** The mic uses the existing `btn btn-sm btn-circle tooltip` pattern (same as send/extra-options), with `data-tip` + `aria-label` for the icon-only control.
- **No API change upwards.** `ChatInputBox`'s public emits are untouched; `upload-files` still carries the audio `File` into `Chat.vue → ChatAttachment.fromFile`.

## 5. Accessibility checklist

- [x] Icon-only mic has both `data-tip` (DaisyUI tooltip) and `aria-label`.
- [x] Recording state is a `role="status"` / `aria-live="polite"` region with `tabular-nums` timer.
- [x] Attach/Cancel are labelled (`aria-label`) and color-independent — accept is `btn-primary`, cancel is `btn-ghost text-error` with an `xmark` glyph.
- [x] Mic is `:disabled` while `waiting` or `readOnly` (DaisyUI keeps the focus ring).
- [x] `Escape` still cancels the recording (document-level listener added by the recorder).
- [x] Touch targets: `btn btn-sm btn-circle` ≥ 32px with `gap-2` spacing (8px minimum between targets).
